        "content": "{\"message\":\"\u2705 Referral opportunity 'Success LLC Referral' has been created for Alex Thompson. You can now share the referral link or details with your colleagues. Let me know if you need anything else!\"}",
        "tool_calls": null
      },
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "That's great news! Thank you for setting that up so quickly. I'll make sure to share the details with my team at Success LLC. Is there anything specific I should keep in mind when referring them, or any follow-up steps I need to take on my end?"
      },
      {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "{\"message\":\"You\u2019re doing a great job! Here are a few quick pointers to keep the referral process smooth and to help you build even more trust with your team:\\n\\n1. **Share the referral link** \u2013 If you have a unique referral URL or code, give it to each colleague so we can track the referral accurately.\\n2. **Highlight the benefits** \u2013 Remind them that they\u2019ll receive a special discount or credit for each successful sign\u2011up, and that we\u2019ll credit you with a referral bonus once the new account is active.\\n3. **Set expectations** \u2013 Let them know the typical onboarding timeline (usually 2\u20133 business days) and that we\u2019ll be in touch to answer any questions.\\n4. **Follow\u2011up** \u2013 After they sign up, a quick check\u2011in (email or call) can reinforce the relationship and show that we value their business.\\n5. **Keep the conversation open** \u2013 If they have any feedback or suggestions, share it with us. It helps us improve the program and strengthens our partnership.\\n\\nIf you\u2019d like a ready\u2011to\u2011send email template or a custom referral landing page, just let me know and I\u2019ll set that up for you. Otherwise, you\u2019re all set\u2014thanks again for spreading the word!\"}",
        "tool_calls": null
      },
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "That's really helpful, thank you! I'll definitely keep those pointers in mind when I reach out to my team. I think having a ready-to-send email template would be a nice touch to make things even smoother for everyone. Could you go ahead and set that up for me? Once I have that, I'll be ready to start making those introductions."
      },
      {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "{\"message\":\"Here\u2019s a ready\u2011to\u2011send email template you can copy\u2011paste and send to your colleagues. Feel free to tweak any part to match your tone.\\n\\n---\\n**Subject:** Invite to Join Success LLC \u2013 Special Referral Offer!\\n\\nHi [Colleague Name],\\n\\nI hope you\u2019re doing well. I wanted to share an exciting opportunity for you to try our CRM platform, which has been a game\u2011changer for our team at Success\u202fLLC.\\n\\n**Why you\u2019ll love it:**\\n- **Easy onboarding** \u2013 Get started in just a few minutes.\\n- **Customizable dashboards** \u2013 See the metrics that matter most to you.\\n- **Dedicated support** \u2013 We\u2019re here to help every step of the way.\\n\\n**Special referral bonus** \u2013 When you sign up using my referral link (or code), you\u2019ll receive a **[X]% discount** on your first year, and I\u2019ll receive a **$[Y] credit** once your account is active.\\n\\n**How to get started:**\\n1. Click the link below or copy the URL into your browser.\\n2. Follow the quick sign\u2011up steps.\\n3. Let me know if you have any questions \u2013 I\u2019ll be happy to walk you through the setup.\\n\\n[**Referral Link**]\\n\\nLooking forward to seeing you on board! If you\u2019d like a quick demo or have any questions, just reply to this email.\\n\\nBest regards,\\nAlex Thompson\\nManager, Success\u202fLLC\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Tip:** If you prefer a personalized touch, you can add a short note about a specific feature that helped your team. That often makes the invitation feel more relevant.\\n\\nLet me know if you\u2019d like me to generate a unique referral link for you or if there\u2019s anything else I can do to help. Happy referrals!\"}",
        "tool_calls": null
      },
      {
